//!   (random scales 0.01-37, a collinear and a point triangle, a small far-off triangle; query points near, on corners, on edges,
//!   far away). Every row must match bit for bit.
//! - the pruned search equals the exhaustive minimum over all faces (lexicographic on distance bits, then face index) on random soups,
//!   a welded grid sheet (shared vertices and edges: exact ties), duplicated coplanar faces and degenerate faces, for meshes on both
//!   sides of the 400-face switch. Zero compared points fails.
//! - the work per query does not grow with the mesh: on welded grid sheets of 800 to 51200 faces the mean number of per-face
//!   evaluations per query stays under a fixed bound (the exhaustive search would grow 64-fold).
